  "author": "Riddim Rack",
  "description": "Talking formant bass: the Vowel table one octave above a clean sine sub, Mod A (triangle, 1/4, grid-locked) scanning the vowels and shifting the formants while Mod B on the same grid moves a BP12 band with them, light Saturate. Held notes keep talking; short notes catch one vowel. Play: held and tied notes around F1-C2, mono legato. Tweak: Mod A/Mod B Division for the talking speed, Mod A Index amount for the vowel range, Mod A Shift amount for formant size, Filter A Res for nasal bite. Macro plan (not wired yet): Talk = Mod A Index + Shift amount, Mouth = Filter A Freq, Bite = Filter A Res, Dirt = Shaper Amt.",
